    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a high-impact offensive performance today, anchored by the elite matchup awaiting **Gunnar Henderson** (81.87). Facing Sugano, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an exceptional 14% park factor boost and an even stronger 19% SP skill advantage, making him our cornerstone play. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.25) provides a robust secondary anchor, leveraging a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Cantillo. Furthermore, our focus on stolen base efficiency is well-represented by **Sam Antonacci** (62.98), who draws a favorable leadoff spot against Wesneski. While **Luis Robert Jr.** (69.94) and **Coby Mayo** (61.38) also benefit from the favorable matchup against Sugano, their scores remain high despite the latter\u2019s minor platoon drag, reinforcing the overall depth of today\u2019s lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Wade Meckler**, whose 39.15 score narrowly missed the 40-point floor for activation. Despite the historical BvP trends and a favorable wind direction, the looming presence of Schlittler\u2014with an xERA of 2.96\u2014pushed **Wade Meckler** to the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable daily matchups. We are also monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely, particularly for **Miguel Vargas**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; should any of these hitters drop significantly in their respective batting orders, their scores will be subject to revision. \n\nRisks are relatively contained today, though we remain cautious of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (44.34) and **Heliot Ramos** (50.07), both of whom are facing the lower-xERA arm of Detmers. **Heliot Ramos** remains a startable option primarily due to the rare combination of slow opposing pitcher delivery and his speed profile, which provides vital upside in our scarcest category. Outside of the lineup, both **Jacob Wilson** and **Jordan Westburg** remain unavailable on the IL, while **Liam Hicks** was sidelined by a subpar projection score that failed to clear the utility threshold. We are proceeding with a full-strength roster elsewhere to maximize our 5x5 potential.",
